NAME
       getty - open a terminal, prompt for a login name and run login

SYNOPSIS
       getty [tty]

DESCRIPTION
       getty prepares a terminal for use and starts the login process on
       it.  It is normally started by init(1), which respawns it after each
       session ends.

       getty performs the following steps:

         o  creates a new session with setsid(2);
         o  opens the terminal device (/dev/console by default, or the tty
            named on the command line) and makes it the controlling
            terminal;
         o  redirects standard input, output and error to the terminal and
            makes its own process group the terminal's foreground group;
         o  puts the line discipline into canonical mode with echo enabled;
         o  displays the login banner and the "<host> login: " prompt;
         o  reads the login name; and
         o  executes /bin/login, passing the login name as an argument.

       When the login session started by login(1) exits, getty exits too,
       and init(1) starts a fresh getty so the login prompt reappears.

OPTIONS
       tty    The terminal device to operate on.  Defaults to
              /dev/console.

FILES
       /dev/console   default terminal device
       /bin/login     program executed to authenticate the user

SEE ALSO
       login(1), init(1)

AUTHORS
